  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Santhosh vs Vittal Rao.L on 30 June, 2025 Kabc030908382019 Presented on : 11.12.2019 Registered on : 12.12.2019 Decided on : 30.06.2025 Duration : 05y/06m/18ays In The Court Of Xli Addl. Chief Judicial Magistrate At : Bengaluru Presided Over By :Tattanda Damayanti Somayya B.A.,Ll.B., Xli Addl. Chief Judicial Magistrate Bengaluru Dated on this 30th day of June 2025 C.C.No.29465/2019 Complainant : The State by Amruthahalli Police Station -V/s- Accused : Vittal Rao.L., S/o. Lakshman Rao, Aged 41 years, R/at. No.87/2017, 4th cross, Jakkur New Junction, Srirampura, Bengaluru. Date of Commission of 13.01.2018 offence Date of report 13.01.2019 Date of arrest 14.01.2019 Name of the complainant Santhosh Date of commencement of 21.03.2023 recording Evidence Date of closing evidence 11.06.2025 2 C.C.No.29465/2019 Offences complained of U/Sec. 285, 337 of Ipc and Sec.3, 4, 5, 7 of Lpg orders and Sec.3, 7 of Essential Commodities Act. State Represented by Senior Asst. Public Prosecutor Accused Represented by Sri.Lokesh.R.Yadav Advocate. Opinion of the Judge As per final orders Judgment [Delivered on 30.06.2025] The P.S.I of Amruthahalli Police Station has filed charge sheet against the accused for the offences punishable U/Sec. 285, 337 of Ipc, Sec. 3, 4, 5, 7 of Lpg orders and Sec.",
    "facts": "[Delivered on 30.06.2025] The P.S.I of Amruthahalli Police Station has filed charge sheet against the accused for the offences punishable U/Sec. 285, 337 of Ipc, Sec. 3, 4, 5, 7 of Lpg orders and Sec. 3 and 7 of Essential Commodities Act Brief facts of prosecution case is as follows: On 13.01.2019 at 3.30p.m., the accused without obtaining license, illegally, by endangering human life, without providing safety measure was getting filled LPG gas to small cylinders from big cylinders at a shed, which is situated adjacent to Kukkadeshwari Nilaya, 5th cross, Varadaraju layout main road, Amruthahalli and as such, due to his negligence, the cylinder got burst and CW.1 and 2 sustained burn injuries. On the basis of statement given by CW.1 before the medical officer of Axis hospital, the Amruthahalli Police have registered this case against the accused in Cr.No.11/2019. 3. On 14.01.2019, the accused was arrested and produced before the Court. On the same day, the Court enlarged him on bail. 4. After the investigation, the IO filed charge sheet against the accused. The Court has taken cognizance of the offences punishable U/Sec. for the O/P/U/Sec. 285, 337 of IPC, Sec.3, 4, 5, 7 of LPG orders and Sec.3 and 7 of Essential Commodities Act. The Court complied with Sec.207 of Cr.P.C., and furnished charge sheet copy to the accused. 5. The Court framed accusation for the offences punishable U/Sec. 285, 337 of IPC, Sec.3, 4, 5, 7 of LPG orders and Sec.3 and 7 of Essential Commodities Act and recorded the plea of the accused. The accused did not plead guilty. He claimed to be tried. 6. In order to prove its case, the prosecution got examined 5 witnesses as PW.1 to 5 and got marked Ex.P.1 to 6 documents. After the closure of the evidence of the prosecution, this court recorded the statement of the accused U/Sec.313 of Cr.P.C., wherein, he denied the incriminating evidence led against him. He did not choose to lead his defense evidence.",
